WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.634
-I want to get into
all the new things.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.467
But first,
I want to talk about --

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.767
I know you just finished
filming "Ant-Man," okay?

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.968
-Mm-hmm.
-"Ant-Man and the Wasp."

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.234
-It's "Quantumania."
-"Quantumania."

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.033
-Uh-huh.
-It's just one name.

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.701
-One name. "Quantumania."
-Just "Quantumania."

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.033
-"Quantumania."
-Yeah.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.300
These Marvel movies,
I mean, also, like --

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.501
-Crazy quantum...

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:24.067
-It's so many quantums
that it's Quantumania.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.167
-Yes.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:26.334
-That's how many --
That's why they --

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.234
There's too many quantums
to talk about.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:32.133
Now, when you signed up for
the first quantum...

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.167
Kind of, right?
-Okay, I'll go with that.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.634
-Thank you. You'll go with that.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.501
You do the first "Ant-Man,"
and you go, "Oh, this is cool."

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:39.801
And you're in that film.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:42.634
Does Marvel tell you that you're
going to be another --

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.300
You're gonna leap...

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.067
Does Marvel explain
to you that --

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:49.467
how many quantums
you're in, possibly?

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:51.634
Is there any -- No.
-No. No.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.868
They're very mysterious.
-Yes.

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:56.667
-And, you know,
they're very secretive,

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:57.934
of course, of their story lines
and all of that.

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.300
-They're so secretive.
-So secretive.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.467
-But I kind of like that.
Well, it must be hard for you.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:07.367
-It's a little hard, because,
you know, I met with Peyton,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.501
and I knew a little bit
about the character,

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:11.834
but there was no script.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:16.701
And they -- And you have to
commit without actually

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:17.868
having read anything.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:20.133
-Have you ever done that before?
-No.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:23.000
-Wow! That's -- You have
a lot of faith there.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.467
-I did.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:29.501
But, you know, it's kind of --
And it wouldn't have mattered,

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.701
because it all changes anyway.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:34.367
So, yeah, it's sort of you
don't really know

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:37.434
what you're getting into,
and then you get a script

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.167
sort of right before
you start shooting and then --

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:41.300
-And it all changes.
-And then it changes every day.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.834
And so --
And then you shoot the movie

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:46.534
and you wrap,
and then it changes again.

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:47.934
-Well, you do that on
"Saturday Night Live," too.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.701
I remember when I was on
that show, they go,

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.567
"Don't memorize your scripts."

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.601
Because they change
every last minute.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.501
And if you're, like, going like,
"I'm going to get the milk,"

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.400
they're like,
"No, we cut that milk bit."

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.467
So if you had memorized
that line, that makes no sense.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.067
-It's so nerve-ra--
I mean, for me,

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.267
it's just so nerve --
I'm not improvisational.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.267
I'm not -- Yeah.
-Really?

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:06.267
-No.

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.267
-You just --
You study your lines

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.567
and you go hit your mark
and nail it.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.100
-I'm very controlling.
-Yeah. You are very controlling.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.701
I know you have a
very talented husband, as well,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.734
David E. Kelley.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.133
-Mm-hmm.
-Man, he's on fire again.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:18.334
-Yeah, he is.

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.868
-He kind of never went --
He's always been on fire,

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.033
but he's crushing it.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.300
-I know.
-Would you ever work with him?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.133
Would you ever work together?
-No.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:28.534
-Perfect. Alright, great.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:32.367
-No, I mean, I --
You know, I'm --

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.734
I mean, the way --
Nobody writes, honestly,

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.100
better for women than he does.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.601
-He's unbelievable, by the way.
-He's unbelievable.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:41.133
-He is a talented, talented guy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.834
He really is, yeah.

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:47.100
-And, yet,
I value our relationship

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.400
more than a good part,
and I just think it's too risky.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.701
And I think -- And, you know,

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:54.734
we're both kind of fierce
when we work.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:59.200
And so if I come home and
I've had a bad day

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.000
and I'm upset
about something, you know,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.133
I want him to be on my side,

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:06.434
because he hasn't heard
the other side.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.567
-That's really funny.
-You know?

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:09.300
-That's very funny.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.601
Yeah, he hasn't heard
the other side.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.767
If he knows
the other side, he'll go,

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:12.767
"Well, wait a second.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:13.934
It wasn't that bad."

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.868
-There's value in that.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.567
-Exactly right.
That's very, very smart.

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.334
How did you guys meet?

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:20.367
-It was a blind date.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.367
-Reals?
-Yeah.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.767
-Blind date with
Michelle Pfeiffer?

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:25.734
-I'm not good left
to my own devices, so...

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:26.834
Yeah, my --

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.934
-Did he freak out?
I would freak out.

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.067
-I think he was --

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.234
-If you went to a blind date
and you go,

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.601
"Your blind date is
Michelle Pfeiffer" --

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:35.734
-No, I mean, he knew it was me.
It's not blind like that.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.767
-Oh. Not like a reality show?

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.501
-No. No. No. Can you imagine?

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:44.000
-Someone set you up -- like
a dinner party or something-ish.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.167
Was it one-on-one?

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.367
-Mm...no.
-Ooh!

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:50.801
-I thought it was
a good idea to --

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.467
I was kind of nervous, I guess.

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:55.767
And I'd had
a couple of bad blind dates.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:59.567
And I had sworn off of them,
and my best friend said,

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:03.467
"Please, just this last time,
meet this guy, David Kelley."

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:04.901
I said, "Okay."

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:11.667
So, I thought it was a good idea
to do, like, a bowling party.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:14.834
-Wow! Really?

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.801
-Not a good idea?
-I don't know. Yeah, maybe.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:19.200
I guess you have to
kind of give it --

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.000
I mean,
bowling is very vulnerable.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.501
-Anyway...

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:24.767
-Wearing other people's shoes.
I mean, it's a whole thing.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.767
-So, then we all met
for dinner before...

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.934
-I like bowling.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.567
-...which was
the awkward part, probably.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:31.868
I think the bowling part
was okay.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:34.133
But then he --
Somehow, he ended up

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.467
sitting across from my sister,
and I ended up

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.767
sitting across from
his best friend.

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.934
And he and my sister were just
chatting it up, you know,

00:04:41.934 --> 00:04:43.000
because she's --
you know, she's --

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.167
-Charming.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.267
-She's very charming
and really good socially.

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.000
I'm not so good.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.067
And he's a little bit shy.
We're both a little bit --

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:51.167
-So you're looking at
your sister like,

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:52.767
"Hey, calm it down
a little bit."

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.567
-No, no.

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.267
No, I say to my best friend,

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:58.000
"I think I should
set Dedee up with him.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.300
They seem to be
really hitting it off."

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.334
She said, "Don't you dare.
I will kill you."

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:07.234
Anyway, she said, "I'm sitting
across from your next husband."

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:09.534
-Your sister said that?
-My best friend said that to me.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.067
-She knew it.
-She knew it.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.901
-Wow.
-We hadn't spoken two words.

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:14.501
I don't know how
she thought that,

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:15.801
but that was our --

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:20.000
-But she was right, huh?
-So it didn't start off great.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.434
-Yeah. But how many years
have you been married?

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:23.801
-It'll be 29 this year.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.467
-Yeah, not too shabby.
There you go.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:27.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
She was right. She was right.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:30.667
-She was right.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:33.734
-Every time you come on,
I gush over you backstage.

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:37.167
But I will gush
in front of stage

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:40.934
and just say that you have
so many iconic roles.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.934
You were just in the news
because the new Catwoman,

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:45.033
Zoe Kravitz, was out.

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:46.367
Everyone is
talking about Catwoman,

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:47.868
and everybody's like,
"Michelle Pfeiffer is, like --

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:50.367
I mean, the bar
has been set, you know?"

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:52.400
And I was like,
"Well, yeah --" I go --

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.601
I mean,
you were phenomenal in that.

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:56.601
And I checked your Instagram,
and there you are

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:58.701
with the cat -- with the whip.

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:00.601
And you still have the whip.
-I do.

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:03.567
-You took it --
You stole it from the set.

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.100
[ Laughter ]
And...

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:09.467
-No.
-You were given it.

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:12.067
-It was my practice whip.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.067 --> 00:06:14.167
-How would you know
the difference?

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:15.167
Do you know which one
was -- Please.

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.501
-No, there's your hero whip...

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:17.567
-Okay. Ooh!

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:19.100
-...and then there's your
practice whip.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.234
-Oh, that's your -- Oh, you got
to keep the practice whip.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.167
-Yeah. So -- Yeah.
-You put in the time.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.033
I mean, you were
actually unbelievable.

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:27.400
-I'm a little rusty,
if you looked at the clip.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.434
-But, yeah -- But, no,
we actually have a clip

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:33.901
from when you were doing
"Batman Returns."

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.234
-Mm-hmm.
-Look at this video.

00:06:35.234 --> 00:06:36.400
Watch Michelle Pfeiffer.

00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:39.934
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.367
How you doing?

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.567
Oh! Come on, now!

00:06:48.868 --> 00:06:50.701
And you got smoke coming out.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:53.234
What are you doing? Come on.

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:54.801
I want you to have
the hero whip now.

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:56.234
-That was so fun.

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:58.367
-I mean, I want to talk about
"The First Lady" -- okay? --

00:06:58.367 --> 00:06:59.634
when we come back, okay?

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:01.467
More with Michelle Pfeiffer,
everybody. Come on back.

